<title>GERMANY: German institutes detail East, West German economic forecasts.</title>
<headline>German institutes detail East, West German economic forecasts.</headline>
<text>
<p>1996	1997	1998</p>
<p>WEST GERMAN DATA:</p>
<p> Gross domestic product (real)    +1.3	+2.25     +2.75</p>
<p> Numbers in work ('000)	     28,186    27,960    28,085</p>
<p>  Unemployed ('000)		    2,796     3,000     2,875</p>
<p>  Unemployment rate (pct)	    9.0	 9.7	 9.3</p>
<p> Consumer prices			+1.4	+1.5	+1.75</p>
<p> Unit wages costs		     -0.4	-1.0	-0.5</p>
<p>EAST GERMAN DATA:</p>
<p> Gross domestic product (real)    +2.0	+2.0	+2.5</p>
<p> Numbers in work ('000)		6,279     6,150     6,135</p>
<p>  Unemployed ('000)		    1,169     1,280     1,285</p>
<p>  Unemployment rate (pct)	   15.7	17.2	17.3</p>
<p> Consumer prices			+2.2	+1.75     +1.75</p>
<p> Unit wages costs		     UNCH	-1.0	UNCH</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
</text>
